pkg:Evidence_v1_9_0 a quality:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Gate transcript for code-abundance-rdodi v1.9.0 (MINOR release)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "MINOR: comprehensive status pass ahead of a kick-off readiness assessment. Found and closed one real gap first -- dependsOn was discussed 2 turns ago (dependency-based, not date-based planning) but never actually built before the session pivoted; built it now across all 5 Stories (STORY-2->1, STORY-3->{1,2}, STORY-4->3, STORY-5->{3,4}), transitive property, no cycle. Re-verified: pipeline order unaffected, full SHACL 0 violations, no dependency-cycle violation fired. Full lineage status confirmed live, not from memory: Mission Out_InFlight (8/8 mission shapes satisfied); Scope 3 Areas/3 Deliverables/3 Exclusions, correct fillsScope direction, ProductScopeKind-tagged; Goals 8/8 per G29's own closure test; Objectives 8, each with real baseline/target, zero with checkpoints (correctly deferred, no real planning basis exists yet to ground one); Backlog 1 Epic/5 Stories, all Proposed, all notYetScoreable, dependency graph now real. Current gate reality re-checked live: 18/18 mechanical RDODI gates pass; Cross.A and Cross.D both genuinely fail today, both now owned (STORY-4, STORY-5 respectively); Epic/Scope fit-gap closed as of v1.8.1. What remains before a legitimate kick-off, stated plainly rather than fabricated ahead of time: prioritise the 5 Stories; size a real Iteration by capacity; commit dependency-resolved, capacity-fitting work via a PlanningEvent; only then declare KickOff, dated to the real moment, never backfilled."@en ;
    pub:transcriptSHA256 "da0d15ca2d0158b6adba59f9cb7eef35342a8a497054e468b74d6aab18f1ad2d"^^xsd:string .
